    {
      "description": null,
      "keys": [
        {
          "default": "spawns",
          "description": "Completeness tier for the audit log. Higher tiers add forensic / analytics value at the cost of DB growth and supervisor-thread overhead.  decisions = only proxy-evaluated events (today's historical behaviour). spawns    = + a compact row for every routine ProcessSpawn short- circuit (find, grep, ls, base64, …). Answers \"what binaries did this session execute?\" with modest write volume. Default. io        = + compact rows for routine file reads / writes. Forensic- ish; ~+100 MB/day under typical dev workloads. all       = + compact rows for noise-path events (/proc/, /dev/null, /var/cache/, CA cert dirs, …). Best for compliance / SIEM exports; requires retention tuning (~+500 MB/day).  Compact rows omit filter_results / filter_scores / composite_score and carry only the call type, supervised pid + tool, and a short argument summary. The dashboard hides them by default; toggle \"Show routine activity\" on the audit page to reveal them.",
          "name": "completeness",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "path": "audit"
